# Product complex KP, seeded from the product-side IRC endpoint (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8).
#
# The IRC from the verified TS ran both directions but hit MaxIter 20 without
# reaching a minimum ("MAXIMUM NUMBER OF ITERATIONS REACHED - STOPPING IRC RUN",
# twice). Its backward branch is the product side: C129-O136 closes from the
# TS's 1.820 A to 1.547 A and the ketone C129=O130 weakens from 1.265 to 1.319.
# That endpoint is job.xyz here, copied verbatim from ../irc/job_IRC_B.xyz.
#
# What the IRC also showed, and what it corrects: the coordinate is dominated by
# the C129-O136 bond, NOT the water relay. The proton that moves is H135 (on the
# attacking O136) -- it stretches off O136 (1.129 at the TS, 1.501 at the
# product endpoint, nearest O134) -- while H131 stays on water1 (O132) at ~0.98 A
# throughout BOTH directions. So H131 is an H-bond spectator here, not the relay
# proton.
#
# This optimisation resolves where the protons actually end up and gives KP,
# which is the missing G(PC): needed for C8's dGdeg gate (-6 to -10 kJ/mol) and
# for the reverse barrier, dG_rev = G(TS) - G(PC).
#
# Same tier as everything else: 20-atom QM region, GFNFF topology, charge 0.
! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ddCOSMO(Water) opt freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136 137 138 139}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
Recalc_Hess 50
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
